course: dictionary
lesson: 667
title: Baker and bakery
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A baker is a person whose job is to make bread, cakes and pies to sell. You can often work out this meaning from the words around it. In «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes», the list shows that the baker is the one who bakes the bread.
explain: Baker is a noun, so it can change to bakers when there is more than one. A bakery is the place where a baker works, and it is often a shop. Baker and bakery are from the same family of words, so if you know one, you can guess a little about the other.
explain: Not every baker works in a shop. Anyone who likes to bake at home can also be called a baker. In a story, «the baker's» usually means the shop, not the person, so read the sentence carefully to see which meaning fits.
fact: A baker is a person who makes bread, cakes and pies to sell.
fact: «The baker's» means the shop where bread and cakes are sold.
fact: A baker's dozen means 13, not 12.
fact: Bakers often work early in the morning, so the bread is fresh for the day.
fact: Bakers use warmth to help yeast make dough rise, and a cold fridge makes it rise very slowly, which can make it tastier.
exercise: «In prison Joseph explained the dreams of Pharaoh's baker and cupbearer.» Who is a baker in this sentence? | A driver who delivers bread | A farmer who grows wheat | A prisoner who sleeps all day | *A person who makes bread and cakes
exercise: What does «a baker's dozen» mean? | 10 | 100 | *13 | 12
exercise: «A farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes, a driver delivers.» Which person bakes the bread? | A miller | *A baker | A farmer | A driver
test: What is a bakery? | A kind of flour | A type of oven | *The place where a baker works | A person who makes pies
test: Which is the right plural of baker? | bakerses | bakery's | bakeres | *bakers
exam: Read this: «Warmth makes yeast work faster, so dough is left somewhere warm; in a cold fridge it rises very slowly, which bakers use to make it tastier.» Why might bakers put dough in a fridge? | To make it rise faster | *To make it rise slowly, which can make it tastier | To freeze it solid | To keep it warm all day
